.\" arise(1) - Gentoo Package Manager
.\" Maintained for the development command surface
.TH ARISE 1 "2026-07-24" "arise development" "Gentoo Package Manager"

.SH NAME
arise \- an experimental recovery-oriented package manager for Gentoo Linux

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B arise
[\fIglobal-flags\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIargs...\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B arise
is an experimental statically-linked Go control plane that aims to provide
compatible workflows for
.BR emerge (1),
.BR eix (1),
.BR equery (1),
.BR quickpkg (1),
.BR perl-cleaner (1),
.BR python-updater (1),
.BR dispatch-conf (1),
.BR env-update (1),
.BR revdep-rebuild (1),
and
.BR eselect-news (1).

It stores package metadata in a BadgerDB key-value store and operates directly
against the Gentoo repository tree and VDB, without depending on Python or Bash
for core operations. Build phases that require shell scripts execute via
\fBos/exec\fR to the appropriate build tools (make, bash, patch, etc.).
Live-root install, update, reinstall, and uninstall execute directly after a
verified plan. Explicit install targets are selected into world unless
\fB\-\-oneshot\fR is set. Saved plans remain available for optional
state-bound review and deferred execution. Source transactions use isolated
phase workers, durable logs, operation locking, package journals, and resumable
dependency-aware scheduling. Depclean and broader maintenance mutation remain
unavailable. Live package management remains experimental and the overlay
release is testing-keyworded for \fB~amd64\fR; keep Portage installed as the
reference and recovery implementation.

The design priorities are correctness, usefulness, performance, and
reliability.  Repair planning is intended to derive and verify a complete
ordered closure instead of requiring administrators to widen manual
\fB\-\-oneshot \-\-nodeps\fR batches by trial and error.  Indexed immutable
state and Go concurrency are used to reduce control-plane latency without
weakening determinism or final-state verification.

.SH OPTIONS

.SS Global Flags
These flags apply to all commands and must precede the command name.
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fIpath\fR
Database path (default: \fI/var/lib/arise/data\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fIpath\fR
Repository path (default: \fI/var/db/repos/gentoo\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-repo-url\fR \fIurl\fR
Remote repository URL for sync operations.

.SS Package Flags
These flags apply to \fBinstall\fR, \fBupdate\fR, and \fBdepclean\fR.
.TP
\fB\-1\fR, \fB\-\-oneshot\fR
Install without adding to the world set.
.TP
\fB\-O\fR, \fB\-\-nodeps\fR
Skip dependency resolution. Install only the specified packages.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-onlydeps\fR
Only install dependencies, not the target packages themselves.
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-emptytree\fR
Rebuild the entire dependency tree as if nothing is installed.
.TP
\fB\-D\fR, \fB\-\-deep\fR
Consider the full dependency tree, not just direct dependencies.
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-update\fR
Update packages to the best available version.
.TP
\fB\-N\fR, \fB\-\-newuse\fR
Rebuild packages when USE flags have changed.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-pretend\fR
Dry run. Display what would be done without performing actions.
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-ask\fR
Prompt for confirmation before performing actions.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non-essential output.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase output verbosity.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-tree\fR
Display the dependency tree instead of a flat list.
.TP
\fB\-j\fR \fIN\fR, \fB\-\-jobs\fR \fIN\fR
Number of parallel build jobs (default: 1).
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-usepkg\fR
Use binary packages when available, falling back to source.
.TP
\fB\-K\fR, \fB\-\-usepkgonly\fR
Only use binary packages. Fail if a binary package is unavailable.
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-buildpkg\fR
Build binary packages during installation.
.TP
\fB\-B\fR, \fB\-\-buildpkgonly\fR
Only build binary packages, do not install.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-fetchonly\fR
Only fetch source files, do not build.
.TP
\fB\-\-backtrack\fR \fIN\fR
Maximum backtracking decisions for dependency resolution (default: 20).
.TP
\fB\-\-resolver-timeout\fR \fIDURATION\fR
Wall-clock resolver deadline (default: \fI5m\fR). A value of \fI0\fR disables
the wall-clock limit without changing the independent backtrack ceiling.
.TP
\fB\-\-approve-plan-sha256\fR \fIDIGEST\fR
Optionally require exactly the displayed canonical verified-plan digest. The digest is
bound to VDB, world, configuration, selected recipes and inherited eclasses;
state drift before execution fails closed.
.TP
\fB\-\-save-plan\fR \fIPATH-OR-NAME\fR
Save the complete generated JSON plan for later inspection and approval.
.TP
\fB\-\-approve-plan\fR \fIPATH-OR-NAME\fR
Optionally require execution to match an exact saved plan. The current package
and policy state is revalidated before mutation.
.TP
\fB\-\-preflight-only\fR
Validate every planned package without fetching, building, or mutating.
.TP
\fB\-\-journal-dir\fR \fIPATH\fR
Directory containing durable package transaction journals.
.TP
\fB\-\-complete-graph\fR
Rebuild reverse dependencies when packages change.
.TP
\fB\-\-keep-going\fR
Continue as much as possible after an error.
.TP
\fB\-\-reinstall\fR
Force reinstall of already-installed packages.
.TP
\fB\-\-changed-use\fR
Reinstall when USE flags differ from current settings.
.TP
\fB\-\-changed-deps\fR
Reinstall when dependency specifications have changed.
.TP
\fB\-\-noreplace\fR
Do not reinstall the exact same version if already installed.
.TP
\fB\-\-resume\fR
Resume the last interrupted operation.
.TP
\fB\-\-skipfirst\fR
Skip the first package when resuming (used with \fB\-\-resume\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-autounmask-write\fR
Write necessary package.unmask and package.license entries when resolution
fails.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fIy|n\fR
Enable or disable colored output (default: terminal auto-detect).
.TP
\fB\-\-unordered-display\fR
Display results in resolution order rather than sorted.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR \fILOAD\fR, \fB\-\-load-average\fR \fILOAD\fR
Pause when system load average exceeds the given value.
.TP
\fB\-\-getbinpkg\fR
Download binary packages from configured binhosts.
.TP
\fB\-\-getbinpkgonly\fR
Only use downloaded binary packages.
.TP
\fB\-\-binpkg-respect-use\fR
Respect USE flag compatibility when selecting binary packages.
.TP
\fB\-\-with-bdeps\fR \fIy|n|auto\fR
How to handle build dependencies (default: n).
.TP
\fB\-\-ignore-built-slot-operator-deps\fR \fIy|n\fR
Ignore slot operator rebuilds (default: n).
.TP
\fB\-\-plan-dir\fR \fIPATH\fR
Directory used for named saved plans.
.TP
\fB\-\-resume-file\fR \fIPATH\fR
Path containing resumable package-action state.
.TP
\fB\-\-work-dir\fR \fIPATH\fR
Package build and transaction workspace.
.TP
\fB\-\-fetch-jobs\fR \fIN\fR
Concurrent source fetch and verification jobs.
.TP
\fB\-\-show-estimates\fR
Show advisory historical per-package and serial-total merge-time estimates.

.SS Search Flags
.TP
\fB\-\-name-only\fR
Search only package/category names, not descriptions.
.TP
\fB\-\-desc\fR
Search descriptions.
.TP
\fB\-\-installed\fR
Only show installed packages.
.TP
\fB\-\-exact\fR
Exact match instead of substring.
.TP
\fB\-\-regex\fR
Use regular expression patterns.
.TP
\fB\-\-category\fR \fIcat\fR
Filter by category.
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fIpkg\fR
Filter by package name.
.TP
\fB\-\-slot\fR \fIslot\fR
Filter by SLOT.
.TP
\fB\-\-use\fR \fIflags\fR
USE flag filter (\fI+flag\fR required, \fI\-flag\fR excluded).
.TP
\fB\-\-keywords\fR \fIkw\fR
Filter by KEYWORDS.
.TP
\fB\-\-license\fR \fIlic\fR
Filter by LICENSE.
.TP
\fB\-\-stable\fR
Only stable-keyworded packages.
.TP
\fB\-\-testing\fR
Only testing-keyworded packages.
.TP
\fB\-\-sort\fR \fIorder\fR
Sort by: category, name, version, slot.
.TP
\fB\-\-compact\fR
Compact output format.
.TP
\fB\-\-versions\fR
Show all available versions.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fIfmt\fR
Custom format string with template variables.
.TP
\fB\-\-print\fR \fIfields\fR
Print specific fields.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output results as JSON.
.TP
\fB\-\-brief\fR
Brief single-line output.
.TP
\fB\-\-only-names\fR
Only output package names.
.TP
\fB\-\-count-only\fR
Only output result count.
.TP
\fB\-\-and\fR
Combine multiple queries with AND logic.
.TP
\fB\-\-not\fR \fIpattern\fR
Exclude packages matching this pattern.
.TP
\fB\-\-world\fR
Only packages in the @world set.
.TP
\fB\-\-system\fR
Only packages in the @system set.
.TP
\fB\-\-depends-on\fR \fIatom\fR
Packages that depend on this.
.TP
\fB\-\-required-by\fR \fIatom\fR
Packages required by this.
.TP
\fB\-\-has-use\fR \fIflag\fR
Packages with this USE flag available.
.TP
\fB\-\-has-version\fR \fIpat\fR
Packages with version matching glob pattern.
.TP
\fB\-\-care\fR
Show packages needing attention (masked, overflow, etc.).
.TP
\fB\-\-overflow\fR
Only show packages with masked keywords.
.TP
\fB\-\-masked\fR
Only show masked packages.
.TP
\fB\-\-duplicates\fR
Show all versions of each package.
.TP
\fB\-\-dump\fR
Dump output in eix-compatible format.

.SH COMMANDS

.SS Package Management

.TP
\fBinstall\fR [\fIflags\fR] \fIatoms...\fR
Resolve, build, install, and select one or more packages. Use
\fB\-\-oneshot\fR to suppress world selection. \fB\-\-pretend\fR displays the
verified plan without mutation; \fB\-\-preflight-only\fR additionally validates
recipe and execution policy without running build tools.

.TP
\fBupdate\fR [\fIflags\fR] [\fIatoms...\fR]
Resolve and execute updates. If no atoms are specified, resolve @world.

.TP
\fBuninstall\fR [\fIflags\fR] \fIatoms...\fR
Verify and execute journaled removal. Use \fB\-\-pretend\fR for a read-only
proposal.

.TP
\fBdepclean\fR [\fIflags\fR]
Propose orphan removal without mutation.

.TP
\fBprune\fR [\fIflags\fR]
Propose old-version removal without mutation.

.TP
\fBdeselect\fR \fIatom\fR
Remove a package from the @world set without uninstalling it.
.TP
\fBselect\fR \fIatom\fR
Add exactly one installed package atom to the @world set using locked,
state-bound mutation.
.TP
\fBrecover status\fR
List durable package transaction journals and their states.
.TP
\fBrecover rollback\fR \fIid\fR
Roll back one active journal while holding the VDB mutation lock. Use
\fB\-\-all-active\fR instead of an identifier to recover every active journal.

.SS Query and Information

.TP
\fBsearch\fR [\fIflags\fR] [\fIquery\fR]
Search the package database. Accepts all search flags listed above and provides
an experimental eix/emerge-search-compatible workflow.

.TP
\fBinstalled\fR [\fIall|repo|no-repo|buildtime|no-buildtime\fR]
[\fB\-\-versions\fR|\fB\-\-cpv\fR] [\fB\-\-null\fR]
[\fB\-=\fR] [\fB\-q\fR] [\fB\-a\fR]
List installed package atoms. The default output is one versionless
\fIcategory/package\fR atom per line. Use \fB\-\-versions\fR (or
\fB\-\-cpv\fR) for \fIcategory/package-version\fR; use \fB\-\-null\fR
for NUL-delimited scripting output. Replaces \fBeix-installed\fR.
The compatibility selectors filter packages by VDB metadata. \fB\-=\fR prefixes
atoms with an equals sign, \fB\-q\fR suppresses explanatory text, and
\fB\-a\fR is shorthand for quiet \fBall\fR output.

.TP
\fBquery\fR \fIatom\fR
Look up metadata for a specific package from the database.
Display description, homepage, license, and other cached metadata.

.TP
\fBstate\fR \fIsubcommand\fR
Emit deterministic available or installed package state for parity, snapshot,
and differential workflows.

.TP
\fBinfo\fR
Display system information: arise version, Go runtime, portage configuration
(CFLAGS, USE, MAKEOPTS, CHOST, FEATURES), active profile, and repository status.
Equivalent to \fBemerge \-\-info\fR.

.TP
\fBequery\fR \fIsubcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR]
Package query tool replacing \fBequery\fR(1). Subcommands:
.RS
.TP
\fBbelongs\fR \fIfile\fR
Find which installed package owns a file.
.TP
\fBfiles\fR \fIatom\fR
List files installed by a package.
.TP
\fBuses\fR \fIatom\fR
Show IUSE and active USE flags for a package.
.TP
\fBsize\fR \fIatom\fR
Show total installed size of a package.
.TP
\fBcheck\fR \fIatom\fR
Verify installed files against recorded checksums.
.TP
\fBwhich\fR \fIatom\fR
Find the ebuild path for a package.
.TP
\fBlist\fR [\fIpattern\fR]
List installed packages matching a pattern.
.RE

.SS Maintenance

.TP
\fBsync\fR
Synchronize the Gentoo repository. Uses \fBgit\fR(1) as primary method with
\fBrsync\fR(1) fallback, then atomically publish the refreshed resolver index.
Success means both stages completed. Requires \fB\-\-repo-url\fR to be set.

.TP
\fBindex\fR
Rebuild the metadata database from the ebuild tree. Walks the md5-cache
directory in parallel and ingests all package metadata into BadgerDB.

.TP
\fBaudit\fR \fIpython|perl\fR [\fIflags\fR]
Audit installed packages for outdated Python or Perl site-packages.
With \fB\-\-fix \-\-pretend\fR, list the affected rebuild set. Non-pretend
\fB\-\-fix\fR remains gated and fails explicitly.
Replaces \fBpython-updater\fR and \fBperl-cleaner\fR.

.TP
\fBpreserved-rebuild\fR [\fIflags\fR]
Scan for broken shared library links and rebuild affected packages.
Equivalent to \fBemerge @preserved-rebuild\fR.

.TP
\fBrevdep-rebuild\fR [\fIflags\fR]
Full reverse dependency scan for broken ELF dependencies.
Replaces \fBrevdep-rebuild\fR(1).

.TP
\fBbench\fR
Run Arise's built-in microbenchmark report. Correctness-gated external
comparisons use the dedicated performance harness.

.SS System Configuration

.TP
\fBdispatch-conf\fR
Recursively review protected configuration updates. Supports the familiar
update, zap, skip, edit, merge, diff, toggle, and quit decisions; automatic
handling of identical, masked, and configured trivial updates; rotated
archives; and configuration-update hooks. Optional path arguments restrict
the scan to specific protected directories or files. Honors
\fBCONFIG_PROTECT\fR, \fBCONFIG_PROTECT_MASK\fR, \fBEROOT\fR,
\fBROOT\fR, and \fI/etc/dispatch-conf.conf\fR.
Provides a usable replacement workflow. It includes safe three-way premerge,
confined atomic archives, mixed-file diffs, and interruption-aware processing.
Session rollback/recovery and broader command-level differential parity remain
under development.

.TP
\fBenv-update\fR
Regenerate \fI/etc/profile.env\fR and \fI/etc/csh.env\fR from \fI/etc/env.d/\fR.
Replaces \fBenv-update\fR(1).

.TP
\fBldconfig\fR
Update the shared library linker cache.
Delegates to \fB/sbin/ldconfig\fR when available.

.TP
\fBconfig\fR \fIatom\fR
Run the \fBpkg_config\fR phase for an installed package.

.TP
\fBnews\fR [\fIsubcommand\fR]
Display Gentoo news items (GLEP 42). Subcommands:
.RS
.TP
\fBlist\fR
List all available news items.
.TP
\fBread\fR
Display unread news items.
.TP
\fBdisplay\fR \fIitem\fR
Display a specific news item.
.RE

.SS Binary Packages

.TP
\fBquickpkg\fR \fIatom\fR
Create a binary package (.tbz2) from an installed package.
Replaces \fBquickpkg\fR(1).

.SH FILES

.TP
\fI/var/lib/arise/data\fR
BadgerDB database directory storing package metadata.

.TP
\fI/var/tdb/repos/gentoo\fR
Default Gentoo repository path.

.TP
\fI/var/tdb/pkg\fR
VDB directory with per-package CONTENTS, USE, IUSE, and environment files.

.TP
\fI/etc/portage/\fR
Portage configuration directory (make.conf, package.use, etc.).

.TP
\fI/var/cache/binpkgs\fR
Binary package cache directory.

.TP
\fI/var/lib/portage/world\fR
World set file listing user-requested packages.

.TP
\fI/var/tmp/arise\fR
Temporary build working directory.

.TP
\fI/var/tmp/arise/resume\fR
Resume state file for interrupted operations.

.SH ENVIRONMENT

.TP
\fBARISE_DB_PATH\fR
Override the default database path.

.TP
\fBARISE_REPO_PATH\fR
Override the default repository path.

.TP
\fBNO_COLOR\fR
Disable colored output when set to any non-empty value.

.TP
\fBCFLAGS\fR, \fBCXXFLAGS\fR, \fBMAKEOPTS\fR, \fBARCH\fR
Standard build environment variables used during package compilation.

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
0
Success.
.TP
1
General failure (missing dependencies, conflicts, build errors).

